note: Choosing with if, and repeating with loop repeat, loop while and loop each.

set number temperature to 18
if temperature > 25 do:
    print("hot")
else if temperature > 15 do:
    print("mild")
else do:
    print("cold")
end

note: Every value can be a condition. 0, empty, "", [] and {} are false; everything else is true.
print(to_boolean(0), to_boolean("0"), to_boolean([]), to_boolean([0]))

note: and / or stop as soon as the answer is known and give a boolean; ! reverses a condition.
set number hour to 14
if hour >= 9 and hour < 18 do:
    print("open")
end
if !(hour is 14) or hour is 3 do:
    print("never printed")
end

note: loop repeat counts through a range. A loop does not open a scope, so i is still there afterwards.
loop repeat i to 1 ~ 3 do:
    print(i * i)
end
print("after the loop, i is", i)

note: A range runs backwards when the start is larger.
loop repeat k to 3 ~ 1 do:
    print(k)
end

set number n to 1
loop while n < 20 do:
    change n to n * 3
end
print(n)

note: loop each visits list items, map keys and text characters; skip moves on, stop ends the loop.
loop each word in ["red", "", "blue", "stop", "green"] do:
    if word is "" do:
        skip
    end
    if word is "stop" do:
        stop
    end
    print(word)
end

loop each key in {"a": 1, "b": 2} do:
    print(key)
end
loop each ch in "한글" do:
    print(ch)
end
